ui.mmo.unavailable = Player power range: not available. The MMO jar this mod can read is missing or older than the one it was built against.
ui.mmo.own_power = Your own power right now: {power}
ui.mmo.cap_above = Your maximum difficulty {cap} sits above the power ceiling {max}, so far zones can out-scale even a maxed group. That is the supported way to do it.
ui.mmo.cap_below = Your maximum difficulty {cap} sits below the power ceiling {max}. Every group past it meets the same difficulty; raise the maximum to at least {max}.
ui.mmo.cap_equal = Your maximum difficulty {cap} matches the power ceiling {max}: a maxed group meets an even fight at the top and nothing harder.
ui.mmo.floor_mismatch = Your minimum difficulty {min} differs from the power floor {powerMin}; the two scales should start together.
ui.mmo.where = Those numbers are edited on the MMO side, not here: the Power Level page of the MMO admin menu, or mods/mmoskilltree/power-level.json (Clamp.MinPower and MaxPower). The player mitigation ceilings the hit curve is derived against live on the Modifier Clamps page of that same menu, or in mods/mmoskilltree/ability-clamps.json over Server/MMOSkillTree/ModifierClamps, and this mod cannot read them.

